[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"NetSerialize, Custom Struct Replication, and Bandwidth Optimization in Unreal Engine"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Efficient bandwidth management is critical for multiplayer performance in Unreal Engine. While standard struct replication works out of the box, it often transmits unnecessary data, saturating the network. Implementing a custom NetSerialize function allows you to control bit-level serialization, drastically reducing bandwidth usage."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The Problem with Default Struct Replication"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"By default, when you mark a custom struct as replicated inside an Actor, Unreal Engine serializes every property within that struct. If your struct contains a transform, a health value, and several status flags, but only the health value changes, the engine still evaluates or sends more data than necessary depending on your replication setup. Furthermore, default float values are replicated with full 32-bit precision, which is often overkill for gameplay metrics."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating a Custom Struct with NetSerialize"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"To override the default serialization behavior, your custom struct must inherit from FNetDeltaSerializeInfo or implement the NetSerialize function by adding bool NetSerialize(FArchive& Ar, class UPackageMap* Map, bool& bOutSuccess) within its definition."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"USTRUCT(BlueprintType)
struct FOptimizedGameData : public FFastArraySerializerItem
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

    UPROPERTY(BlueprintReadWrite, EditAnywhere)
    float Health = 100.0f;

    UPROPERTY(BlueprintReadWrite, EditAnywhere)
    uint8 Lives = 3;

    bool NetSerialize(FArchive& Ar, class UPackageMap* Map, bool& bOutSuccess)
    {
        Ar.SerializeBits(&Health, 8); // Quantize or limit bits if needed
        Ar.SerializeInt(&Lives, 4);   // Serialize only 4 bits for lives (0-15)
        bOutSuccess = true;
        return true;
    }
};

template<>
struct TStructOpsTypeTraits<FOptimizedGameData> : public TStructOpsTypeTraitsBase2<FOptimizedGameData>
{
    enum
    {
        WithNetSerialize = true,
    };
};
"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Bandwidth Optimization Techniques"},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Bit-Packing: Use Ar.SerializeBits to send exact ranges of data instead of full types (e.g., sending a normalized value from 0 to 1 using fewer bits)."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Conditional Serialization: Check flags within the archive to decide whether specific sub-properties should be sent across the network."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Quantization: Convert high-precision vectors or rotators into compressed integers before serialization."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"By implementing custom NetSerialize routines for your structs, you gain surgical control over what data crosses the wire. This pattern prevents network congestion, reduces packet loss, and ensures a smoother multiplayer experience for fast-paced Unreal Engine titles."}]
